The permanent fix for the moving target that kept the self-proof unreachable
(INV-dabuf G1, plan of record on the item). Every one of hypergumbo's 18
claims governs the INSTALLED CLI - their sources are python cmd_* handlers -
yet the coverage gate demanded an opinion on every external call IN THE REPO.
scripts/auto-pr and repo hooks blocked claims they cannot participate in, and
any new import anywhere re-broke the proof. A target ordinary development
un-hits is unreachable because the denominator MOVES, not because coverage is
thin.

THE BOUNDARY IS PACKAGING METADATA, NOT A PATH LIST. Every pyproject.toml
carrying a [project] table names a package; a package dir that is an ANCESTOR
of another is a workspace wrapper and is dropped (hypergumbo's root pyproject
sits above six real packages - keeping it would widen the scope back to the
whole repo and make the feature a measured no-op on the proof it exists for);
src layout preferred, flat layout falls back to the dir; a flat package AT the
repo root scopes to "." (artifact degrades to production, the correct reading
of a repo that ships everything it contains). This is what separates it from
the reachability scoping rejected on INV-dabuf's thread: that one was computed
by the analysis whose completeness was in question and failed open by
construction. Packaging is checkable independently, and a repo that ships
shell as console entry points keeps it in scope because its own metadata says
so. TOML parsing reuses profile._load_toml (tomllib/tomli fallback) rather
than growing a second loader.

OPT-IN, DISCLOSED, ONE POPULATION. Absent key = today's behaviour
byte-for-byte (pinned by the production-scope control test). The declaration
lives in the claims file a reader audits, and the run prints the kept/total
edge counts and roots on stderr - a verdict must never be quietly narrower
than its claims document. Nodes and edges are filtered TOGETHER: the first run
with edges scoped and nodes not had bash/javascript/typescript read as
"analyzed but produced no call edges", and the analyzer-blind check blocked
every claim on languages the artifact does not contain - INV-sarum's rule,
re-learned live and pinned by
test_a_language_present_only_outside_the_artifact_does_not_blind. An unknown
scope value and a scope with no packaging to bind to are both LOUD rc 2, never
defaulted: a typo silently read as production hands the author back exactly
the denominator they opted out of.

docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml declares the scope, with the rationale in the
file where its reader is.

